@lang en
IMPORT `baominh-par-claim`

-- Tests for the claim as a whole: scenarios in which the three layers interact (cover, then
-- exclusions, then average, contribution, the caps and the deductible, under the conditions).
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the clauses cited, before the assertion was run.
-- Amounts are scenario values in VND.

§ `Tests: the claim`

§§ `Fixtures for the claim`

GIVEN ch IS A LIST OF `A link in the chain of causation`
      v  IS A `The valuation of the item`
GIVETH A `A damaged item`
`the stock, damaged by` ch `valued` v MEANS `A damaged item` WITH
    `the item insured`                  IS `the stock`
    `kind`                              IS stock
    `the chain of causation`            IS ch
    `circumstances`                     IS `the ordinary circumstances`
    `valuation`                         IS v
    `what the Insured told the Insurer` IS `nothing false was said`
    `changes under General Condition 8` IS EMPTY
    `claimed as a cost of changing or adding to a computer system, programme, software or chip` IS FALSE

-- the stock: 100,000,000 of Damage, worth its sum insured of 500,000,000, and another policy of
-- 500,000,000 on it
`the stock's valuation` MEANS `The valuation of the item` WITH
    `the Damage, valued at the time of the loss`                      IS 100000000
    `the part of the Damage arising from a cause not excluded`        IS NOTHING
    `the actual value of the item at the time of the loss`            IS JUST 500000000
    `sums insured by other insurances of the same property or loss`   IS LIST 500000000
    `the amount the marine policy would pay if this policy did not exist` IS NOTHING
    `the costs of the media`                                          IS NOTHING

`the burnt building, under-insured` MEANS
    `an item of` buildings `damaged by` (LIST `directly` fire) `in` `the ordinary circumstances` `valued` (`Damage of` 200000000 `to property worth` 1250000000)

`the burnt stock` MEANS `the stock, damaged by` (LIST `directly` fire) `valued` `the stock's valuation`

`the burnt building` MEANS `a damaged` buildings `by` (LIST `directly` fire)

§§ `Cover, then average and contribution, then the caps and the deductible`

-- building: 200,000,000 x 1,000/1,250 (GC 14)            = 160,000,000
-- stock:    100,000,000 x 500/(500 + 500) (GC 6)          =  50,000,000
-- the loss: 210,000,000, under the total sum insured of 1,500,000,000, less 10,000,000 (GC 13)
#ASSERT `the answer for the claim` `the Schedule` (`a loss of` (LIST `the burnt building, under-insured`, `the burnt stock`)) EQUALS `the Insurer must pay` 200000000

-- an excluded item alongside a covered one: a theft from stock without force (exclusion 1(c)(i))
-- and the ordinary fire in the building: 100,000,000 - 10,000,000
`a fire and a sneak theft` MEANS
    `a loss on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `of` (LIST `the burnt building`, `the stock, damaged by` (LIST `directly` theft) `valued` `the stock's valuation`) `with theft` (JUST (`The circumstances of a theft` WITH `in the insured building` IS TRUE, `with force or violence to break in or to get out` IS FALSE)) `act` NOTHING `dispossession` NOTHING `building empty` NOTHING `conduct` `good conduct` `premium` `the premium paid on time`
#ASSERT `the answer for the claim` `the Schedule` `a fire and a sneak theft` EQUALS `the Insurer must pay` 90000000

-- apportioned: latent defect and fire, 30,000,000 of the Damage from the fire: 30,000,000 - 10,000,000
#ASSERT `the answer for the claim` `the Schedule` (`a loss of the item` (`an item of` buildings `damaged by` (LIST `directly` `latent defect`, `directly` fire) `in` `the ordinary circumstances` `valued` (`Damage of` 100000000 `, of which not excluded` 30000000 `, to property worth` 1000000000))) EQUALS `the Insurer must pay` 20000000

§§ `Nothing payable, and why`

-- General Condition 4(a)
#ASSERT `the answer for the claim` `the Schedule` (`a loss on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `of` (LIST `the burnt building`) `with theft` NOTHING `act` NOTHING `dispossession` NOTHING `building empty` NOTHING `conduct` (`conduct with` (LIST `a fraudulent claim`) `and` `the procedure followed`) `premium` `the premium paid on time`) EQUALS `nothing is payable because` (LIST "General Condition 4(a): the claim is fraudulent in some respect")
-- outside the period of insurance
#ASSERT `the answer for the claim` `the Schedule` (`a loss on` (YMD 2027 2 1) `of` (LIST `the burnt building`) `with theft` NOTHING `act` NOTHING `dispossession` NOTHING `building empty` NOTHING `conduct` `good conduct` `premium` `the premium paid on time`) EQUALS `nothing is payable because` (LIST "insuring clause: the loss was not in the period of insurance or a renewal of it", "the amount for the loss, after the conditions, the caps and the deductible, is nil")
-- an exclusion takes out the only item
#ASSERT `the answer for the claim` `the Schedule` (`a loss of the item` (`a damaged` buildings `by` (LIST `indirectly` war, `directly` fire))) EQUALS `nothing is payable because` (LIST "exclusion 3", "the amount for the loss, after the conditions, the caps and the deductible, is nil")
-- under the deductible
#ASSERT `the answer for the claim` `the Schedule` (`a loss of the item` (`an item of` buildings `damaged by` (LIST `directly` fire) `in` `the ordinary circumstances` `valued` (`Damage of` 5000000 `to property worth` 1000000000))) EQUALS `nothing is payable because` (LIST "the amount for the loss, after the conditions, the caps and the deductible, is nil")
-- General Condition 9(a): notice and measures not immediate
#ASSERT `the answer for the claim` `the Schedule` (`a loss on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `of` (LIST `the burnt building`) `with theft` NOTHING `act` NOTHING `dispossession` NOTHING `building empty` NOTHING `conduct` (`conduct with` EMPTY `and` (`a claims procedure with` (JUST 10) NOTHING FALSE TRUE)) `premium` `the premium paid on time`) EQUALS `nothing is payable because` (LIST "General Condition 9(a)(i): no immediate measures to minimise the loss", "General Condition 9(a)(ii): no immediate written notice to the Insurer")
-- General Condition 12
#ASSERT `the answer for the claim` `the Schedule` (`a loss on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `of` (LIST `the burnt building`) `with theft` NOTHING `act` NOTHING `dispossession` NOTHING `building empty` NOTHING `conduct` (`conduct with` (LIST `poor maintenance`) `and` `the procedure followed`) `premium` `the premium paid on time`) EQUALS `nothing is payable because` (LIST "General Condition 12: the property was not properly maintained")

§§ `The premium warranty in a claim`

-- never paid; a fire on 20 January, inside the 30 days, is covered (fork F27): 100,000,000 - 10,000,000
#ASSERT `the answer for the claim` `the Schedule` (`a loss on` (YMD 2026 1 20) `of` (LIST `the burnt building`) `with theft` NOTHING `act` NOTHING `dispossession` NOTHING `building empty` NOTHING `conduct` `good conduct` `premium` (`the premium paid on` NOTHING)) EQUALS `the Insurer must pay` 90000000
-- never paid; a fire in June is not
#ASSERT `the answer for the claim` `the Schedule` (`a loss on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `of` (LIST `the burnt building`) `with theft` NOTHING `act` NOTHING `dispossession` NOTHING `building empty` NOTHING `conduct` `good conduct` `premium` (`the premium paid on` NOTHING)) EQUALS `nothing is payable because` (LIST "General Condition 15: the cover had been cancelled for non-payment of the premium before the loss")

§§ `A fact the answer needs is missing`

#ASSERT REFUSED `the answer for the claim` `the Schedule` (`a loss of the item` (`a fire damaging but unvalued`)) BECAUSE "the actual value of the item at the time of the loss is not in the record"

`a fire damaging but unvalued` MEANS
    `an item of` buildings `damaged by` (LIST `directly` fire) `in` `the ordinary circumstances` `valued` (`The valuation of the item` WITH `the Damage, valued at the time of the loss` IS 100000000, `the part of the Damage arising from a cause not excluded` IS NOTHING, `the actual value of the item at the time of the loss` IS NOTHING, `sums insured by other insurances of the same property or loss` IS EMPTY, `the amount the marine policy would pay if this policy did not exist` IS NOTHING, `the costs of the media` IS NOTHING)
